WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:03.680
How Meta ads really work, and what a sale is worth to you.

2
00:00:04.030 --> 00:00:08.680
This is the video for module one of Paid Advertising with Meta Ads.

3
00:00:09.930 --> 00:00:20.920
Boosting is a shortcut. Ads Manager is the full workshop. Every ad lives in three levels. The campaign sets the objective, the result Meta should find for you.

4
00:00:22.170 --> 00:00:25.490
The ad set decides who sees it, where, and the budget.

5
00:00:26.740 --> 00:00:31.860
The ad is what people actually see: the image or video, the text and the button.

6
00:00:33.110 --> 00:00:43.120
A common beginner mistake is one campaign per ad. Instead, use one campaign per business goal, one to three ad sets, and three to five ads in each.

7
00:00:44.370 --> 00:00:55.870
Each time someone opens Facebook or Instagram, Meta holds an instant auction. The winner is not simply the highest payer. It combines three things. First, your bid.

8
00:00:57.120 --> 00:01:00.340
Second, how likely this person is to do what you asked.

9
00:01:01.590 --> 00:01:11.740
Third, ad quality. So a relevant ad that people respond to wins more auctions, and each result costs less. A dull or misleading ad pays more.

10
00:01:12.990 --> 00:01:19.690
When an ad set starts, Meta explores who responds. This is the learning phase, and results jump around.

11
00:01:20.940 --> 00:01:32.930
Changing targeting, creative or the event, or a large budget change, sends it back. So plan properly, launch, and leave it alone, unless a link is wrong or an ad is rejected.

12
00:01:34.180 --> 00:01:51.080
Meta's guidance is about 50 events in 7 days to exit learning. Amaka ran 9 tiny campaigns at 2,000 naira a day, so none could get there. She merged them into one Sales campaign at 18,000 naira a day, with her 5 best ads inside.

13
00:01:52.330 --> 00:02:02.760
The objective tells Meta whom to look for. Choose Traffic, and Meta finds people who click. Choose Sales, and it finds people who buy. Often they are different people.

14
00:02:03.110 --> 00:02:12.150
Funmi spends about 35,000 naira on each ad set. The Traffic one gets clicks for just 25 naira, but only 4 purchases.

15
00:02:13.400 --> 00:02:30.240
The Sales one costs more per click, yet brings 11 purchases. Return on ad spend, ROAS, is 5.66 against 2.06. So judge on cost per result and ROAS. Use the cheap numbers only to diagnose why.

16
00:02:31.490 --> 00:02:41.810
Advanced advertisers do the maths before they open Ads Manager. Without a target, you cannot tell if a sale at 4,000 naira is excellent or ruinous.

17
00:02:43.060 --> 00:02:49.610
Kemi's products, packaging, payment fee and delivery subsidy cost 9,070 naira per order.

18
00:02:50.860 --> 00:03:08.350
What is left, 8,930 naira, is the most she can spend to win one order and break even. That is her break-even cost per acquisition, or CPA. Her margin is about 49.6 percent, so her break-even ROAS is about 2.0.

19
00:03:09.600 --> 00:03:21.790
She aims lower, at 5,400 naira, so the business makes real profit. Below ROAS 2.0 she pauses or fixes. Above 3.3 she considers scaling.

20
00:03:23.040 --> 00:03:36.630
If 20 percent of orders are refused at the door, each order is worth only 80 percent of what Meta reports. Meta cannot see WhatsApp sales, so record those yourself. Confirm your card works before launch.

21
00:03:36.980 --> 00:03:49.560
Never let a client borrow for ad spend on a hoped-for ROAS. And scammers send fake policy violation messages. Never enter your password from a link, and turn on two-factor authentication.

22
00:03:50.810 --> 00:04:08.950
To remember. One campaign per goal, with a few well-funded ad sets. Relevance and quality win the auction. Give an ad set room for about 50 events in 7 days. Judge on cost per result and ROAS. And know your break-even CPA before you spend a single naira.

23
00:04:10.200 --> 00:04:25.280
Now practise. Map an account and redraw it with fewer ad sets. Calculate a real report by hand. Then build a unit economics sheet with your break-even CPA, target CPA and the event your budget can support.

24
00:04:25.630 --> 00:04:27.570
Continue with the lessons below.
